I have finally found a solution to the RAID-1 problem that I posted earlier
on the list a while back.  Thanks go to Jay Estabrook @ HP for helping us locate
and find a solution.  The stock 2.4.x kernels with Red Hat are compiled in a
way that produce random Oopses and "unable to handle kernel paging request",
when using software RAID-1 on a DP264.  The solution to this problem is to
add "-fno-strength-reduce" to CFLAGS in arch/alpha/Makefile and recompile
the entire kernel.  Doing this allowed us to get a stable 2.4.19 kernel on
RAID-1, using gcc 2.96.

Hopefully this will help others to get this to work reliably also.

--
Chris
Systems Admin
Group InfoTech, Inc.

