Jan Riis S�rensen wrote:

> Hi
> 
> I just aquired a Digital Alpha Server 1000 4/233. I also don't know the
> password and want to install RH Alpha. My problem is how I get it to boot
> from CD. I know there's a command "Show device" but how do I know which
> one is cd and which is floppy ??
> 

floppy is usually device DV0 and the cdrom is usually DKA400 - if in doubt 
try all devices listed, or if all hard-drives are same type then they will 
all have same drive type on right of list so the CD and Dat-drive will be 
the odd-ones-out so try these first.The CD on mine has a model number 
starting with RD shown on device list if this helps (can't tell you exact 
number as I'm at home and alpha's at work).

One thing to be careful about (which cought me out at first) is that by 
default the drivebays have SCSI ID's counting from ID 0 at the top and on 
my alphaserver the CD is ID4 and the DAT is ID5 so if a hard-drive is 
installed in 5th bay down then CD won't work (a drive in 6th bay down will 
stop dat-drive working).



