(I'm definitely an expert, but I have installed RH 6.1, 7.0, and
7.1 on an SRM machine, so until somebody more informed follows
up...)  The following assumes you are using SRM:

When you boot from the CD, you are using the copy of aboot on the
CD itself.  So, you can install from CD even if your fixed disks
are entirely, completely blank.  (I had to do that after one of
my Seagates died.)  At some point in the installation, the
installer will write aboot to the fixed disk.  After
installation, when you boot from a fixed disk, it will use the
copy of aboot on the fixed disk.

If you really want to do things manually, you can, but you don't
normally have to.  It sounds like it would probably be best to
let the installer do things automagically.

When you partition the disks, make sure to use BSD-style
partitioning and leave a few MB of space free at the start of the
disk.

Did that help answer a few of the questions?

Good luck.

