>> If your system has SRM then don't use milo it.
>> 
> 
> 7.2 installed on my computer with AlphaBIOS, but MILO for some reason would
> not boot it.  Therefore, I switched from AlphaBIOS to SRM and 7.2 is working
> great now.
> 

A default distribution kernel is compiled with LEGACY_LOAD_ADDRESS, or
something of that sort - easy to identify, not set in its kernel
configuration or that kernel would not boot on "wildfire" class
machines.  Therefore you either need a recent milo which can handle such
kernel (yes, versions of milo capable of that do exist but booting via
milo is officially "not supported") or a custom compiled kernel where
this configuration option is set.

If you are booting via SRM/aboot then changes in LOAD_ADDRESS will
be handled transparently.

  Michal


