Does the installation kernel come up?  If so, you can manually
partition the disks using fdisk.  As soon as the installer comes
up, hit ALT-CTL-F2 (IIRC) to get a virtual console with a root
shell.  IIRC, the device nodes are in /tmp/dev rather than /dev.
I have had to do that sort of thing to repair damaged
installations, as long as the installer comes up.

Good luck.

