I never had any problem getting the software, in fact, I never
had to speak to anyone.  Of course, I came from a .edu site at
the time, and there was no HP ownership.
Their development tools flatten GNU.  Their compiler
runs faster and produces better code.  Win, Win.  
Even if there are a few more hoops now than I had to deal with
it's probably worth it.

> -- 2
>We plan on installing Linux (RH 7.1) on a 3-year old alpha
