on Wed, 04 Sep 2002 17:02:08 +0200, Juhana Paavola wrote:
> I'm thinking to buy new big ide disk for storing files.
> But, does PWS onboard IDE controller work with them.
> Does it recognize it, if don't, does it still work under linux ?
> Disk what I'm thinking is Maxtor 100gb/7200rpm/DMAxxx.

I don't know if large disks are supported by PWS IDE controller.
Probably they aren't.
Anyway, the CMD IDE controller is very buggy and requires some software
workaround in linux kernel to work properly.
The IDE controller should work at 16MB/s (no ultradma mode) and the
workaround should lower ide performance, I presume.

To be sure about disk support and to have a good data rate you'd better
buy a (low end) PCI IDE controller, even a DMA66, which is correctly
supported by linux kernel.
Anyway, don't put it into the 64bit PCI slots...

Bye
gl :)


